00:08:36.220 --> 00:08:44.880
I think this is proof why Pam, a new mother and a woman, is reading the body language correctly and no one else is.
我认为这证明了为什么帕姆，作为一位新手妈妈和女性，能正确解读身体语言，而其他人却不能。

151
00:08:44.880 --> 00:08:47.820
Do you think Justin Spitzer had that in mind?
你觉得贾斯汀·斯皮策（Justin Spitzer）当时是这么想的吗？

152
00:08:48.260 --> 00:08:49.300
I doubt it.
我表示怀疑。

153
00:08:49.420 --> 00:08:50.760
But it makes sense.
但这也说得通。

154
00:08:50.940 --> 00:08:53.540
It is backed up by scientific research.
这有科学研究支持。

155
00:08:54.460 --> 00:08:55.500
I loved all of that.
我喜欢所有这些内容。

156
00:08:55.660 --> 00:08:56.120
Did you like that?
你喜欢吗？

157
00:08:56.260 --> 00:08:57.060
I could hear more.
我还能再听听。

158
00:08:57.380 --> 00:08:59.200
Okay, I feel like I've been talking a long time.
好吧，我觉得我说了太久了。

159
00:08:59.720 --> 00:09:05.100
Fast fact number three, Angela is all yours because Angela got in touch with Hide.
第三个速览事实，安吉拉，交给你了，因为安吉拉联系上了秀（Hide）。

160
00:09:05.480 --> 00:09:07.220
Yes, we have been trading messages.
是的，我们一直在互通消息。

161
00:09:07.220 --> 00:09:09.580
We finally connected, and I am so excited.
我们终于联系上了，我太兴奋了。

162
00:09:09.820 --> 00:09:15.180
Well, you know, he had that great talking head and happy hour, and then he comes back again in this episode.
嗯，你知道，他在“欢乐时光”那集里有很棒的采访镜头，然后他又在这集里回归了。

163
00:09:15.360 --> 00:09:15.960
I know.
我知道。

164
00:09:15.960 --> 00:09:22.980
So Hide Toshiomura plays Hide in the warehouse, and I asked him about his time on the show.
秀·托西奥穆拉（Hide Toshiomura）在剧中饰演仓库员工秀，我问了他关于他在剧组工作的事。

165
00:09:23.480 --> 00:09:25.220
He had the most wonderful answers.
他的回答非常精彩。

166
00:09:25.460 --> 00:09:30.360
I'm going to sprinkle them throughout the episode, but I thought I would start with two of the questions I asked him in Fast Fact 3.
我打算把这些回答穿插在整集节目中，但我想先在第三个速览事实里分享我问他的两个问题。

167
00:09:30.700 --> 00:09:30.940
Great.
太棒了。

168
00:09:31.260 --> 00:09:34.200
My first question to Hide was our standard question, Jenna.
我问秀的第一个问题是我们惯例的问题，珍娜。

169
00:09:34.400 --> 00:09:35.960
How did you come to be on the office?
你是怎么加入《办公室》剧组的？

170
00:09:36.340 --> 00:09:37.260
Here's what he said.
他是这么说的。

171
00:09:37.480 --> 00:09:44.140
Way before doing that big talking head, you know, in happy hour, he did background work as an extra for the show.
在拍那个重要的采访镜头之前，你知道，就是在“欢乐时光”那集，他曾作为临时演员在剧里做背景工作。

172
00:09:44.140 --> 00:09:51.100
At that time, he said he had no idea what the show was about, but his manager called him and asked if he wanted to do some work as an extra.
他说当时他根本不知道这部剧是讲什么的，但他的经纪人打电话问他愿不愿意去当临时演员。

173
00:09:51.360 --> 00:09:53.620
So he said, sure, and went along with it.
于是他说，当然愿意，就去了。

174
00:09:54.320 --> 00:09:58.120
After some time of being a background player, his manager called him and said,
在做了一段时间的背景演员后，他的经纪人打电话告诉他，

175
00:09:58.340 --> 00:10:04.740
they want you to audition for an unknown bigger role in the show, like a featured role.
他们想让他去为一个剧里未知的、戏份更重的角色试镜，类似于特约角色。

176
00:10:05.360 --> 00:10:10.940
He said the role wasn't actually defined at the time, so he had no idea what they wanted or what to expect.
他说当时这个角色还没定型，所以他根本不知道他们想要什么，也不知道会发生什么。

177
00:10:10.940 --> 00:10:11.460
Hmm.
嗯。

178
00:10:12.020 --> 00:10:17.160
He went to the audition, and he said there was a wide variety of different people from all backgrounds.
他去参加了试镜，他说现场有各种各样、来自不同背景的人。

179
00:10:17.600 --> 00:10:22.380
He said that when it was time for his audition, he thought he completely botched it.
他说轮到他试镜时，他觉得自己搞砸了。

180
00:10:22.600 --> 00:10:23.060
Oh, no.
噢，不。

181
00:10:23.360 --> 00:10:23.560
Yeah.
是的。

182
00:10:23.740 --> 00:10:32.000
He said he was embarrassed, and he went to his car, and he got in his car, and as he was about to turn it on, he decided, no, I can't let it end like this.
他说他当时很尴尬，就回到了车里，正准备发动车子时，他心想，不，我不能就这样结束。

183
00:10:32.620 --> 00:10:33.060
What?
什么？

184
00:10:33.500 --> 00:10:33.900
Yeah.
是的。

185
00:10:34.140 --> 00:10:38.500
He got out of his car and immediately asked for a re-audition on the spot.
他从车里出来，当场要求再试镜一次。

186
00:10:38.600 --> 00:10:39.400
I love this.
我喜欢这个故事。

187
00:10:39.400 --> 00:10:45.220
Then he said, they were like, sure, and he auditioned again, and he said, I bombed again.
然后他说，他们答应了，于是他又试了一次，他说，我又搞砸了。

188
00:10:45.420 --> 00:10:46.100
Oh, no.
噢，不。

189
00:10:46.840 --> 00:10:56.060
He said he felt defeated, and he went back home, and when he was at his lowest and about to go to bed, he got a call from his manager saying, you got the job.
他说他感到很挫败，回到家，就在他情绪最低落准备上床睡觉时，接到了经纪人的电话，说，你被录用了。

190
00:10:56.380 --> 00:10:57.100
Oh, my gosh.
天哪。

191
00:10:57.100 --> 00:10:59.400
This is every actor's story, I have to say.
我得说，这是每个演员都会有的经历。

192
00:10:59.660 --> 00:10:59.710
Yes.
没错。

193
00:10:59.710 --> 00:11:01.320
How many times has this happened to you?
这种事发生在你身上多少次了？

194
00:11:01.380 --> 00:11:01.860
So many.
太多次了。

195
00:11:01.960 --> 00:11:04.440
You're like, oh, that was horrible, and then they're like, oh, guess what?
你当时觉得，噢，那简直糟透了，然后他们却说，噢，你猜怎么着？

196
00:11:04.480 --> 00:11:04.920
You got it.
你被录用了。

197
00:11:04.920 --> 00:11:08.520
Or you're like, I nailed it, and they're like, we've gone another way.
或者你觉得，我表现得太完美了，他们却说，我们选择了其他人。

198
00:11:09.020 --> 00:11:09.500
Yes.
是的。

199
00:11:09.920 --> 00:11:11.040
So many times.
太多次了。

200
00:11:11.240 --> 00:11:21.540
Well, I remember when they did this audition process, they wanted to fill out the warehouse, and they knew now that the warehouse was going to be more than just background,
嗯，我记得他们进行这个试镜过程时，是想填补仓库的人员，而且他们当时已经知道仓库的角色不仅仅是背景板了，

201
00:11:21.560 --> 00:11:23.880
that they were going to want to throw lines to people.
他们会想要找人来念台词。

202
00:11:23.880 --> 00:11:29.540
So they were trying to fill the warehouse with people who could do speaking roles as well.
所以他们试图在仓库里塞满也能说台词的人。

203
00:11:29.720 --> 00:11:31.240
So I totally remember this.
所以我完全记得这件事。

204
00:11:31.400 --> 00:11:38.280
Well, I also asked Hede if he had any favorite memories from his time on the set, and this is what he shared, and Jenna, it's so sweet.
嗯，我还问了Hede在片场有没有什么难忘的回忆，这是他分享的内容，Jenna，真的太贴心了。

205
00:11:38.420 --> 00:11:38.700
What?
什么？

206
00:11:39.340 --> 00:11:48.940
Here's what he said, and I quote, I finally remember a moment when I had to do ad-libbing on the spot with Jenna for one of the scenes, and even though my English is not very good,
他是这么说的，我引用一下：我终于想起一个瞬间，我得和Jenna在其中一场戏里即兴发挥，尽管我的英语不是很好，

207
00:11:48.940 --> 00:11:53.200
I had a fun time trying my best to keep the conversation going and entertaining.
但我很享受尽力让对话继续下去并保持趣味的过程。

208
00:11:53.500 --> 00:11:57.320
At that moment, I remembered why I love acting so much.
那一刻，我记起了我为什么那么热爱表演。

209
00:11:57.520 --> 00:12:00.480
Oh, that means so much to me.
噢，这对我很重要。

210
00:12:00.820 --> 00:12:01.180
I know.
我知道。

211
00:12:01.580 --> 00:12:02.860
Well, I remember that.
嗯，我记得那件事。

212
00:12:02.860 --> 00:12:06.440
It was in season nine, and he was great.
那是在第九季，他表现得很棒。

213
00:12:06.820 --> 00:12:08.960
I just loved connecting with him.
我真的很喜欢和他交流。

214
00:12:09.080 --> 00:12:11.560
I'm going to share a few more of his stories along the way.
我之后还会分享更多他的故事。

215
00:12:12.200 --> 00:12:21.620
But, lady, before we get into the episode, would you like to know what we were doing the week we filmed this episode in March of 2010?
但是，女士，在进入剧集讨论之前，你想知道2010年3月我们拍摄这一集的那周我们在做什么吗？

216
00:12:21.920 --> 00:12:24.000
Is this a bit of Angela's Digital Clutter?
这是Angela的数字杂物环节吗？

217
00:12:24.180 --> 00:12:25.140
It sure is.
没错。

218
00:12:27.560 --> 00:12:28.940
Angela's Digital Clutter.
Angela的数字杂物。

219
00:12:30.360 --> 00:12:31.200
Thank you.
谢谢。

220
00:12:32.440 --> 00:12:38.320
Apparently, Jenna, I was very into making banana bread during this time.
显然，Jenna，那段时间我非常热衷于做香蕉面包。

221
00:12:38.320 --> 00:12:42.820
And I was bragging to you in an email about my banana bread.
我还在邮件里跟你吹嘘我的香蕉面包。

222
00:12:43.240 --> 00:12:45.300
And I had brought some to set.
我还带了一些到片场。

223
00:12:45.520 --> 00:12:51.260
And you had tried it, and you really liked it, and you emailed me asking me for my banana bread recipe.
你尝过了，而且很喜欢，还发邮件问我要香蕉面包的食谱。

224
00:12:52.160 --> 00:12:55.940
To which I replied, four to five mashed bananas.
我回复说：四到五个捣碎的香蕉。

225
00:12:56.180 --> 00:12:57.680
Use ripe ones.
要用熟透的。

226
00:12:58.140 --> 00:12:59.520
Why did I like it?
为什么我会喜欢它？

227
00:12:59.840 --> 00:13:01.080
Like, you know what?
就像，你知道吗？

228
00:13:01.280 --> 00:13:04.040
A novice banana bread baker wouldn't know.
新手香蕉面包烘焙师可能不知道。

229
00:13:04.280 --> 00:13:04.540
Okay.
好吧。

230
00:13:04.540 --> 00:13:10.420
Then I said, two cups all-purpose flour, one cup sugar, or less if you can't see your toes.
然后我说：两杯通用面粉，一杯糖，如果你看不见自己的脚趾，就少放点。

231
00:13:10.800 --> 00:13:12.240
I'm making jokes here?
我在开玩笑吗？

232
00:13:12.380 --> 00:13:13.920
I'm making jokes in my recipe.
我在食谱里开玩笑。

233
00:13:14.820 --> 00:13:15.960
Comedy recipe.
喜剧食谱。

234
00:13:16.120 --> 00:13:16.480
I know.
我知道。

235
00:13:16.840 --> 00:13:23.640
Two large eggs, half a cup shortening or vegetable oil, one teaspoon baking powder, half a teaspoon salt, one teaspoon vanilla.
两个大鸡蛋，半杯起酥油或植物油，一茶匙泡打粉，半茶匙盐，一茶匙香草精。

236
00:13:24.320 --> 00:13:24.960
Enjoy.
享用吧。

237
00:13:25.720 --> 00:13:27.660
No nuts, no raisins in that.
里面没有坚果，没有葡萄干。

238
00:13:27.820 --> 00:13:28.160
Nope.
没有。

239
00:13:28.540 --> 00:13:29.820
Just pure banana bread.
纯粹的香蕉面包。

240
00:13:30.160 --> 00:13:31.100
Kept it simple.
保持简单。

241
00:13:31.100 --> 00:13:35.620
I hope you're going to post that full recipe in Office Ladies Pod Stories on Instagram.
我希望你会把完整的食谱发到Instagram的Office Ladies Pod Stories上。

242
00:13:35.620 --> 00:13:37.800
I will post it exactly as I emailed it to you.
我会按照我发给你的原样发布。

243
00:13:37.860 --> 00:13:38.320
Very good.
非常好。

244
00:13:39.100 --> 00:13:40.720
Are you still making that banana bread?
你现在还在做那个香蕉面包吗？

245
00:13:40.900 --> 00:13:43.580
I am, except now I do one other thing with it.
还在做，只是现在我多加了一道工序。

246
00:13:43.820 --> 00:13:44.080
What?
什么？

247
00:13:44.300 --> 00:13:46.800
I put a little powdered sugar on top.
我在上面撒了一点糖粉。

248
00:13:47.160 --> 00:13:47.600
Oh.
噢。

249
00:13:47.860 --> 00:13:51.720
At the end, you know, after you've let it cool, put a little powdered sugar on top.
最后，你知道，等它冷却后，在上面撒一点糖粉。

250
00:13:51.840 --> 00:13:55.160
Are you allowed to do that if you can see your toes only?
如果你只能看见自己的脚趾，你还能这么做吗？

251
00:13:55.420 --> 00:13:56.100
I guess not.
我想也是。

252
00:13:56.260 --> 00:13:58.660
And sometimes I put mini chocolate chips in it.
有时候我还会往里面加点迷你巧克力豆。

253
00:13:58.920 --> 00:13:59.240
Oh.
哦。

254
00:13:59.480 --> 00:13:59.880
I know.
我知道。

255
00:13:59.880 --> 00:14:02.220
It really has graduated to more of a treat.
它真的已经升级成一种更棒的甜点了。

256
00:14:02.500 --> 00:14:03.040
I know.
我知道。

257
00:14:03.760 --> 00:14:05.120
Well, let's take a break.
好吧，我们休息一下。

258
00:14:05.120 --> 00:14:14.440
And when we get back, I have some very interesting inter-office memos between our show and NBC's Standards and Practices.
回来之后，我会分享一些我们节目组和NBC审查部门之间非常有趣的内部备忘录。

259
00:14:14.760 --> 00:14:15.900
Oh, I can't wait.
哦，我等不及了。

260
00:14:25.020 --> 00:14:25.680
All right.
好的。

261
00:14:25.800 --> 00:14:28.400
Well, this episode starts with a very chipper Michael.
这一集开始时，迈克尔非常兴奋。

262
00:14:28.820 --> 00:14:34.200
He is going to greet Erin in Spanish and insist that she answers the phone in Spanish.
他打算用西班牙语问候艾琳，并坚持让她用西班牙语接电话。

263
00:14:34.200 --> 00:14:37.160
He's very excited about speaking Spanish.
他对说西班牙语感到非常兴奋。

264
00:14:37.160 --> 00:14:42.520
Well, he has a talking head where he says that he believes everyone should learn Spanish.
他在一段采访中说，他认为每个人都应该学习西班牙语。

265
00:14:43.140 --> 00:14:45.380
He has a lot of thoughts about it.
他对此有很多想法。

266
00:14:45.520 --> 00:14:49.260
And then he says, oh, also, I'm going on vacation to Cancun next week.
然后他说，哦，对了，下周我要去坎昆度假。

267
00:14:49.260 --> 00:14:49.780
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

268
00:14:51.040 --> 00:14:52.860
Who is he going on vacation with?
他是和谁一起去度假的？

269
00:14:53.060 --> 00:14:53.980
I know.
我知道。

270
00:14:54.300 --> 00:14:55.400
By himself?
他一个人去吗？

271
00:14:55.760 --> 00:14:56.740
To Cancun.
去坎昆。

272
00:14:57.220 --> 00:14:58.400
I thought it was odd.
我觉得这很奇怪。

273
00:14:58.580 --> 00:14:59.200
I know.
我知道。

274
00:14:59.620 --> 00:15:01.760
Well, he holds up a little brochure.
他举起了一本小册子。

275
00:15:02.080 --> 00:15:05.540
That was designed by our graphic designer, Henry Sane.
那是我们的平面设计师亨利·塞恩设计的。

276
00:15:05.840 --> 00:15:07.660
You know, he was very busy this week.
你知道，他这周非常忙。

277
00:15:08.260 --> 00:15:10.140
I'm going to point it out throughout the episode.
我会在这一集中不断指出这一点。

278
00:15:10.300 --> 00:15:13.960
He made a lot of stuff, starting with Fakie Cancun brochure.
他做了很多东西，首先就是那本假的坎昆宣传册。

279
00:15:14.440 --> 00:15:15.080
Ding, ding, ding.
叮，叮，叮。

280
00:15:15.220 --> 00:15:16.680
Number one, Henry Sane tracker.
第一项，亨利·塞恩追踪记录。

281
00:15:17.220 --> 00:15:20.860
Well, Michael is now going to go up to Jim and speak Spanish.
迈克尔现在要去找吉姆说西班牙语了。

282
00:15:20.860 --> 00:15:21.900
And guess what?
你猜怎么着？

283
00:15:22.100 --> 00:15:23.520
Jim is really good.
吉姆说得非常好。

284
00:15:23.900 --> 00:15:27.400
Which is curious because we had a fan catch from Elsa N.
这很奇怪，因为我们收到了一位来自犹他州的粉丝艾尔莎·N以及其他许多人的反馈，他们说，

285
00:15:27.540 --> 00:15:29.620
in Utah and many others who said,
在第四季第15集《夜出》中，当清洁工来打扫办公室需要离开停车场时，吉姆让奥斯卡帮忙翻译。

286
00:15:29.620 --> 00:15:36.740
in Night Out, Season 4, Episode 15, Jim asks Oscar to translate when the cleaning crew comes
然而，在《肢体语言》那一集中，吉姆说了好几句西班牙语，

287
00:15:36.740 --> 00:15:39.580
to clean the office and they need to be let out of the parking lot.
这让你觉得他其实说得挺好的。

288
00:15:40.380 --> 00:15:44.000
However, in body language, Jim says multiple sentences in Spanish,
嗯。

289
00:15:44.000 --> 00:15:46.520
which makes you think he can speak it pretty well.
看来有人没在看剧本设定。

290
00:15:47.160 --> 00:15:47.680
Huh.
我想也是。

291
00:15:48.100 --> 00:15:50.060
Someone was not following the show, Bible.
另外，还有一个来自波多黎各的粉丝哈尼·O的提问。

292
00:15:50.360 --> 00:15:51.440
I guess not.
我有一个关于西班牙语的发现，每次看这一集都让我很困扰。

293
00:15:52.140 --> 00:15:56.020
Also, though, fan question from Honey O in Puerto Rico.
在开场戏中，吉姆在迈克尔面前炫耀他的西班牙语，但他说了，

294
00:15:56.860 --> 00:16:00.860
I have a Spanish catch that bothers me every time I watch this episode.
“Yo soy fantastico”（我是个很棒的人）。

295
00:16:01.200 --> 00:16:05.740
In the cold open, Jim is showing off his Spanish to Michael, but then he says,
在吉姆问迈克尔过得如何的特定语境下，

296
