德怀特不明白为什么达里尔突然得到了这个机会，而他却没有。

621
00:30:12.260 --> 00:30:15.940
He points out a number of ways that he himself is a minority.
他列举了许多自己属于少数群体的理由。

622
00:30:15.940 --> 00:30:20.740
He wears glasses, he's a cholera survivor, and he's a genius.
他戴眼镜，是霍乱幸存者，还是个天才。

623
00:30:21.200 --> 00:30:23.360
And a non-organic family farmer.
而且还是个非有机家庭农场主。

624
00:30:24.000 --> 00:30:24.820
Genius.
天才。

625
00:30:25.580 --> 00:30:25.780
Mm.
嗯。

626
00:30:26.260 --> 00:30:26.480
Hmm.
嗯。

627
00:30:26.820 --> 00:30:26.900
Hmm.
嗯。

628
00:30:27.340 --> 00:30:28.200
Really, Dwight.
真是够了，德怀特。

629
00:30:28.660 --> 00:30:29.360
Interesting.
有意思。

630
00:30:29.980 --> 00:30:41.860
But Dwight's big takeaway from this meeting with Gabe and Daryl is that he does not want a competent, hard worker like Daryl to get this job.
但德怀特从这次与盖博和达里尔的会面中得出的主要结论是，他不想让达里尔这样能干、努力的员工得到这份工作。

631
00:30:42.360 --> 00:30:46.480
He wants somebody who he can manipulate, and that means Kelly.
他想要一个他能操纵的人，那就是凯莉。

632
00:30:47.360 --> 00:30:47.660
Yeah.
没错。

633
00:30:48.000 --> 00:30:53.700
Dwight thinks with this program, Daryl might get Michael's position or higher, and that's what Dwight has wanted.
德怀特认为通过这个项目，达里尔可能会得到迈克尔的职位甚至更高的职位，而那正是德怀特一直想要的。

634
00:30:53.900 --> 00:30:54.260
Yeah.
是啊。

635
00:30:54.380 --> 00:30:56.880
So he's got to sabotage him in his mind.
所以在他看来，他必须搞破坏。

636
00:30:57.220 --> 00:30:57.880
That's right.
没错。

637
00:30:57.880 --> 00:31:00.940
So he's going to go over to Kelly's desk, and he's going to tell her about the program.
所以他打算走到凯莉的办公桌前，把这个项目告诉她。

638
00:31:01.780 --> 00:31:03.200
Random background catch.
随机背景发现。

639
00:31:03.420 --> 00:31:11.580
If you look past Kelly's bedazzled saber water bottle, you can see a candle that someone has wedged two thumbtacks into.
如果你越过凯莉那个镶满水钻的赛博水瓶看过去，能看到一支蜡烛，有人往上面插了两枚图钉。

640
00:31:11.920 --> 00:31:12.980
You know those people.
你懂那种人。

641
00:31:13.180 --> 00:31:15.080
Those people that have to stick something in a candle.
那种非得往蜡烛上插点什么的人。

642
00:31:15.840 --> 00:31:16.580
Oh, yeah.
哦，是啊。

643
00:31:16.800 --> 00:31:16.960
Yeah.
是啊。

644
00:31:17.120 --> 00:31:18.040
Now that you say it.
你这么一说还真是。

645
00:31:18.180 --> 00:31:18.380
Yeah.
是啊。

646
00:31:19.000 --> 00:31:20.320
I mean, what is that?
我是说，那到底是什么意思？

647
00:31:20.440 --> 00:31:21.020
I don't know.
我不知道。

648
00:31:21.200 --> 00:31:21.940
I've done it.
我干过这事儿。

649
00:31:22.500 --> 00:31:26.040
I have an irony alert in this scene.
这一幕里有个讽刺警报。

650
00:31:26.360 --> 00:31:26.800
Irony?
讽刺？

651
00:31:26.980 --> 00:31:27.400
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

652
00:31:27.400 --> 00:31:27.880
Okay.
好的。

653
00:31:28.640 --> 00:31:33.640
Dwight looks at Kelly and says, how many Indian CEOs can you think of?
德怀特看着凯莉说，你能想到多少位印度裔首席执行官？

654
00:31:34.340 --> 00:31:38.260
Well, my friends, I think we're looking at one, Ms. Mindy Kaling.
好吧，朋友们，我想我们正看着其中一位，明迪·卡灵女士。

655
00:31:38.620 --> 00:31:39.100
Yes.
没错。

656
00:31:39.300 --> 00:31:41.580
She has her own media company, Kaling International.
她有自己的传媒公司，卡灵国际。

657
00:31:41.580 --> 00:31:43.220
I know she's president for sure.
我确定她是总裁。

658
00:31:43.360 --> 00:31:48.260
She may not be CEO, but I mean, please, to the queen that is Mindy Kaling.
她可能不是首席执行官，但我的意思是，拜托，向明迪·卡灵这位女王致敬。

659
00:31:48.620 --> 00:31:49.240
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

660
00:31:49.400 --> 00:31:49.780
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

661
00:31:49.920 --> 00:31:56.380
I want you to know there was a deleted scene between Dwight and Gabe later in the episode where Dwight says the same thing to Gabe.
我想让你们知道，这一集后面还有一段德怀特和盖博被删减的戏，德怀特对盖博说了同样的话。

662
00:31:56.380 --> 00:31:58.920
How many Indian CEOs can you name?
你能说出多少位印度裔首席执行官的名字？

663
00:31:59.140 --> 00:32:00.780
And Gabe lists off a whole bunch.
然后盖博列举了一大堆。

664
00:32:01.260 --> 00:32:02.280
I love that.
我喜欢这个。

665
00:32:02.860 --> 00:32:07.000
Back in the conference room, Michael is now going to take over like he does.
回到会议室，迈克尔现在要像往常一样接管局面了。

666
00:32:07.300 --> 00:32:09.620
He's got a whole slideshow ready to go.
他准备好了一整套幻灯片。

667
00:32:09.960 --> 00:32:19.480
Yeah, but what Michael is projecting are a series of images that go back and forth between Michael and, I guess, things intended to turn Donna on.
是啊，但迈克尔投影出来的是一系列图片，在迈克尔和我猜是旨在让唐娜兴奋的东西之间来回切换。

668
00:32:19.620 --> 00:32:19.960
Yeah.
没错。

669
00:32:20.180 --> 00:32:21.520
Here's Michael's talking head.
这是迈克尔的单人访谈。

670
00:32:21.720 --> 00:32:23.220
He says, it's subtle.
他说，这很微妙。

671
00:32:23.420 --> 00:32:24.420
That's how it works.
这就是它的运作方式。

672
00:32:24.420 --> 00:32:30.200
I show her an image that turns her on, and then she looks at me, then back at me, then back at the image.
我给她看一张让她兴奋的图片，然后她看着我，再看回我，再看回图片。

673
00:32:30.380 --> 00:32:32.560
Soon, she doesn't know what is me and what is the image.
很快，她就分不清哪个是我，哪个是图片了。

674
00:32:32.700 --> 00:32:34.660
She just knows that she's turned on.
她只知道自己很兴奋。

675
00:32:35.160 --> 00:32:35.420
Yes.
是的。

676
00:32:35.600 --> 00:32:38.180
And then the last slide quickly just says sex.
然后最后一张幻灯片上直接写着“性”。

677
00:32:38.420 --> 00:32:38.720
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

678
00:32:39.620 --> 00:32:39.880
Hmm.
嗯。

679
00:32:40.680 --> 00:32:47.060
This whole scene made me think of a college advertising class I had where we talked about subliminal messaging.
整个场景让我想起了大学时上过的一门广告课，我们讨论过潜意识信息。

680
00:32:47.440 --> 00:32:51.580
Lady, we had that class in my high school, and I wrote my senior paper on the subject.
大姐，我高中时就上过那门课，我还写过关于这个主题的毕业论文呢。

681
00:32:51.780 --> 00:32:52.680
Oh, my gosh.
天哪。

682
00:32:53.420 --> 00:33:00.480
Well, I have nothing new to share with you then, Jenna, but I will tell you, here are a few things I found online, and I'm sure you can add to it.
好吧，珍娜，那我没什么新东西可以分享了，但我会告诉你，这是我从网上找到的一些资料，我相信你能补充一些。

683
00:33:01.160 --> 00:33:08.280
According to a website called HubSpot, subliminal messaging and advertising is designed to engage people subconsciously.
根据一个叫HubSpot的网站，潜意识信息和广告旨在潜意识地吸引人们。

684
00:33:08.280 --> 00:33:17.900
These ads use various colors, shapes, and words that enable customers to make a small but powerful association between a brand and an intended meaning.
这些广告使用各种颜色、形状和文字，使顾客能够在品牌和预期含义之间建立一种微小但强有力的联系。

685
00:33:18.180 --> 00:33:22.020
As I looked up subliminal messaging, Jenna, one guy's name kept coming up.
当我搜索潜意识信息时，珍娜，有一个人的名字一直出现。

686
00:33:22.260 --> 00:33:22.540
Who?
谁？

687
00:33:22.880 --> 00:33:24.720
James McDonald Vickery.
詹姆斯·麦克唐纳·维克里。

688
00:33:25.100 --> 00:33:26.040
What did he do?
他做了什么？

689
00:33:26.240 --> 00:33:27.400
Get ready for this.
准备好听这个吧。

690
00:33:27.620 --> 00:33:32.060
The whole concept of subliminal messaging was first introduced by him.
潜意识信息的整个概念最初就是由他提出的。

691
00:33:32.060 --> 00:33:34.440
He was a marketing researcher, and in 1957,
他是一位市场研究员，在1957年，

692
00:33:34.440 --> 00:33:46.320
he claimed that he did an experiment in which moviegoers were repeatedly shown a 1,000-3,000-second advertisement saying something to the effect of,
他声称自己做了一个实验，让电影观众反复观看一段1000到3000分之一秒的广告，内容大意是，

693
00:33:46.480 --> 00:33:48.580
hungry, eat popcorn, drink Coca-Cola.
饿了，吃爆米花，喝可口可乐。

694
00:33:49.000 --> 00:33:58.300
Based on these claims, the CIA got involved and did a report called the Operational Potential of Subliminal Perception in 1958
基于这些说法，中央情报局介入并于1958年发布了一份名为《潜意识感知的作战潜力》的报告，

695
00:33:58.300 --> 00:34:02.320
that led to subliminal cuts being banned in the U.S.
这导致潜意识剪辑在美国被禁止。

696
00:34:02.680 --> 00:34:03.180
Wow.
哇。

697
00:34:03.420 --> 00:34:05.620
The CIA suggested that, quote,
中央情报局指出，引用如下：

698
00:34:05.940 --> 00:34:13.680
certain individuals can at certain times and under certain circumstances be influenced to act abnormally without awareness of the influence.
某些人在特定时间和特定环境下，可能会在没有意识到这种影响的情况下，被诱导做出异常行为。

699
00:34:13.960 --> 00:34:14.400
Wow.
哇。

700
00:34:14.720 --> 00:34:16.520
So here's the twiSt.
所以，反转来了。

701
00:34:17.160 --> 00:34:22.800
Vickery provided no explanations for his results or any other details about his study to the public,
维克里没有向公众提供任何关于其研究结果的解释或细节，

702
00:34:22.980 --> 00:34:25.520
claiming it was part of a confidential patent.
声称这是保密专利的一部分。

703
00:34:25.520 --> 00:34:32.080
Years later, Stuart Rogers interviewed the theater where Vickery supposedly conducted the experiment,
多年后，斯图尔特·罗杰斯采访了维克里据称进行实验的那家电影院，

704
00:34:32.620 --> 00:34:36.720
and the theater manager said that no such test ever happened at that theater.
电影院经理表示，那家电影院从未进行过此类测试。

705
00:34:37.180 --> 00:34:37.800
What?
什么？

706
00:34:38.120 --> 00:34:46.740
In a television interview in 1962 for Advertising Age, Vickery admitted that the original study was a gimmick
在1962年接受《广告时代》的电视采访时，维克里承认最初的研究只是个噱头，

707
00:34:46.740 --> 00:34:51.200
and that the amount of data was too small to be meaningful.
而且数据量太小，没有意义。

708
00:34:51.200 --> 00:34:55.120
After this interview, Vickery shied away from media attention,
这次采访后，维克里开始回避媒体的关注，

709
00:34:55.360 --> 00:34:58.100
but his papers are held by the Thomas J.
但他的文件被保存在康涅狄格大学的托马斯·J·多德研究中心。

710
00:34:58.300 --> 00:35:00.660
Dodd Research Center at the University of Connecticut.
自那以后，关于这件事的评论和理论层出不穷。

711
00:35:01.020 --> 00:35:05.640
There have been many commentaries and theories about this since it happened.
但我认为这很迷人。

712
00:35:05.920 --> 00:35:08.120
But I thought that was fascinating.
这似乎反驳了潜意识广告的有效性。

713
00:35:08.420 --> 00:35:13.220
That seems to disprove subliminal advertising works.
就像是个骗局一样。

714
00:35:13.580 --> 00:35:15.100
Like it was a hoax.
没错，正是如此。

715
00:35:15.100 --> 00:35:17.080
Yes, exactly.
据称，维克里承认他从未进行过那项潜意识实验，

716
00:35:17.700 --> 00:35:21.820
Supposedly, Vickery admitted that he never conducted the subliminal experiment,
那只是为了吸引客户到他濒临倒闭的营销公司而搞的噱头。

717
00:35:22.440 --> 00:35:26.600
and it was a gimmick to attract customers to his failing marketing business.
天哪。

718
00:35:27.000 --> 00:35:28.600
Oh my gosh.
我知道，但这引发了关于市场营销和广告的全面讨论，

719
00:35:28.760 --> 00:35:34.460
I know, but it started a whole conversation about marketing and advertising
以及如何吸引人们关注你的品牌并建立联想。

720
00:35:34.460 --> 00:35:37.880
and how to attract people to your brand and make associations.
这让我找到了一堆讨论潜意识信息和公司标志的网站，

721
00:35:38.520 --> 00:35:44.440
This led me to a bunch of websites that talked about subliminal messagings and company logos,
我想分享几个我最喜欢的。

722
00:35:44.440 --> 00:35:47.300
and I want to share a few of my favorites.
好的。

723
00:35:47.600 --> 00:35:47.940
All right.
你知道Tostitos薯片吗？

724
00:35:48.720 --> 00:35:50.440
You know the Chips Tostitos?
知道。

725
00:35:50.840 --> 00:35:51.140
Yep.
好的。

726
00:35:51.520 --> 00:35:51.720
Okay.
那你有没有注意到Tostitos中间的两个字母“T”是两个朋友在分享薯片和莎莎酱？

727
00:35:51.960 --> 00:36:00.020
So have you ever noticed that the two T's in the middle of Tostitos are two friends sharing chips and salsa?
是的。

728
00:36:00.440 --> 00:36:01.040
Yes.
我觉得这太可爱了。

729
00:36:01.440 --> 00:36:02.980
I thought that was so cute.
我儿子曾经非常痴迷于标志和标志里的隐藏信息。

730
00:36:02.980 --> 00:36:09.440
My son got really obsessed with logos and hidden messages in logos.
所以大约一年前，我几乎每个周六和周日都会陪他看标志，

731
00:36:09.640 --> 00:36:17.100
So about a year ago, I would spend pretty much every Saturday and Sunday looking at logos with him
并讨论其中的隐藏信息。

732
00:36:17.100 --> 00:36:18.720
and talking about the hidden messages.
这曾是我育儿生活中的重要组成部分。

733
00:36:18.720 --> 00:36:22.620
This was like a big part of my parenting life for a while.
嗯，我的孩子们给我看了芭斯罗缤的标志。

734
00:36:22.840 --> 00:36:25.340
Well, my kids showed me the Baskin-Robbins one.
提醒我一下。

735
00:36:25.780 --> 00:36:26.620
Remind me.
好的。

736
00:36:26.780 --> 00:36:26.980
Okay.
你看，蓝色的部分写着Baskin-Robbins。

737
00:36:26.980 --> 00:36:30.580
So in blue, you know, it says Baskin-Robbins.
这家店以销售31种口味的冰淇淋而闻名。

738
00:36:30.820 --> 00:36:34.420
The store is famous for selling 31 flavors of ice cream.
如果你看标志中非蓝色的粉色部分，你会发现在字母B和R里藏着一个3和一个1。

739
00:36:34.420 --> 00:36:41.740
And if you look at the non-blue part of the logo that's pink, you can see a 3 and a 1 within the B and the R.
哦，这个不错。

740
00:36:41.920 --> 00:36:43.360
Oh, good one.
我知道。

741
00:36:43.620 --> 00:36:44.060
I know.
好了，再看一个。

742
00:36:44.320 --> 00:36:45.380
Okay, here's another one.
联邦快递的标志在字母E和X之间有一个箭头。

743
00:36:45.500 --> 00:36:48.980
The FedEx logo has an arrow between the E and the X.
是的。

744
00:36:49.120 --> 00:36:49.540
Yes.
那是用白色勾勒出来的。

745
00:36:49.800 --> 00:36:51.180
That's outlined in white.
也许是为了展示公司的速度和交付能力。

746
00:36:51.700 --> 00:36:54.580
Maybe that's to show the company's speed and delivery.
嗯哼。

747
00:36:54.820 --> 00:36:55.100
Mm-hmm.
那个箭头。

748
00:36:55.100 --> 00:36:55.640
The arrow.
亚马逊，非常容易辨认的标志。

749
00:36:56.340 --> 00:36:58.360
Amazon, very recognizable logo.
如果你注意看，有一个黄色的箭头从A指向Z。

750
00:36:58.720 --> 00:37:03.260
If you notice, there is a yellow arrow that points from the A to the Z.
没错。

751
00:37:03.920 --> 00:37:09.120
And, you know, I'm guessing here the messaging is that they sell everything from A to Z, right?
而且，你知道，我猜这里的寓意是他们什么都卖，从A到Z，对吧？

752
00:37:09.260 --> 00:37:09.600
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

753
00:37:09.820 --> 00:37:11.560
So those were a few of my favorites.
以上就是我最喜欢的几个片段。

754
00:37:11.720 --> 00:37:22.220
But it's a very interesting concept or idea about logos and marketing and brands and what we retain from this messaging and if it works with brand association.
但关于标志、营销、品牌，以及我们从这些信息中记住了什么，还有它是否通过品牌联想发挥作用，这是一个非常有趣的概念或想法。

755
00:37:22.820 --> 00:37:23.960
Well, what do we think?
那么，我们怎么看？

756
00:37:23.960 --> 00:37:26.460
Do we think Donna is picking up on Michael's messages?
你们觉得唐娜领会到迈克尔传达的信息了吗？

757
00:37:27.200 --> 00:37:28.020
I think.
我觉得领会到了。

758
00:37:28.020 --> 00:37:29.100
How can you not?
怎么可能没领会呢？

759
00:37:30.940 --> 00:37:34.100
I have a little slideshow breakdown for you.
我为你们准备了一个简短的幻灯片解析。

760
00:37:34.220 --> 00:37:35.020
Oh, I'd love it.
哦，我太想看了。

761
00:37:35.020 --> 00:37:36.960
Courtesy of Randy Cordray.
由兰迪·科德雷提供。

762
00:37:37.200 --> 00:37:42.840
At 6 minutes and 21 seconds, you see a photo of a muscled man in his underwear.
在6分21秒处，你看到了一张穿着内裤的肌肉男照片。

763
00:37:43.200 --> 00:37:50.840
This was a licensed stock photo purchased for $350 from Getty Images, and the model's name was Raymond Hemings.
这是一张从盖蒂图片社以350美元购买的授权库存照片，模特的姓名是雷蒙德·赫明斯。

