这段采访镜头还有糖果袋的备选台词。

925
00:44:43.360 --> 00:44:48.080
Here was one that didn't make it, but that Ed had to deliver as Andy.
这是其中一段没用上的，但艾德必须以安迪的身份说出来。

926
00:44:48.920 --> 00:44:50.720
How do I know a girl's interested?
我怎么知道一个女孩对我感兴趣？

927
00:44:50.960 --> 00:44:57.000
I call her up on stage, get down on one knee, and sing Sign Your Name by Terrence Trent Darby.
我会把她叫上台，单膝跪地，唱特伦斯·特伦特·达比的《Sign Your Name》。

928
00:44:57.260 --> 00:44:58.660
Then I give her a rose.
然后送她一朵玫瑰。

929
00:44:58.980 --> 00:45:01.900
If she's interested, she'll find me at the CD table.
如果她感兴趣，她会来CD摊位找我。

930
00:45:02.340 --> 00:45:02.780
Huh.
哈。

931
00:45:03.800 --> 00:45:06.720
So how many times did he sing to a gal in a cappella?
所以他到底在无伴奏合唱团里给女孩唱过多少次歌？

932
00:45:06.920 --> 00:45:07.720
I don't know.
我不知道。

933
00:45:07.920 --> 00:45:10.220
And then go and wait for her at the CD table.
然后去CD摊位等她。

934
00:45:10.920 --> 00:45:15.880
Now Donna is going to inquire about a discount, but when she does, she takes her jacket off.
现在唐娜要询问折扣的事了，但当她开口时，她脱掉了外套。

935
00:45:15.980 --> 00:45:21.520
And I felt like Michael had that same moment that everyone had at Coachella when Harry Styles took his coat off.
我觉得迈克尔那一刻的反应，和大家在科切拉音乐节看到哈里·斯泰尔斯脱掉外套时的反应一模一样。

936
00:45:22.000 --> 00:45:23.080
That was a moment.
那真是一个名场面。

937
00:45:23.720 --> 00:45:25.320
Who's with me in the sound booth?
录音室里有谁跟我有同感吗？

938
00:45:25.520 --> 00:45:26.440
It was a moment.
那确实是个名场面。

939
00:45:27.180 --> 00:45:28.260
Cassie, I see you.
凯西，我看到你了。

940
00:45:28.260 --> 00:45:32.620
It was muted, but Cassie giggled immediately is the correct response.
虽然静音了，但凯西立刻笑了出来，这才是正确的反应。

941
00:45:35.520 --> 00:45:41.420
Well, this causes Michael to make a promise he can't really keep, which is that he's going to give her this discount.
好吧，这导致迈克尔做出了一个他其实无法兑现的承诺，那就是他要给她这个折扣。

942
00:45:42.240 --> 00:45:46.980
But he goes over to check with Oscar, who's running the numbers, and Oscar says,
但他过去找奥斯卡核实，奥斯卡正在算账，奥斯卡说，

943
00:45:47.140 --> 00:45:51.760
Michael, we will literally lose money if we sell the printers at that price.
迈克尔，如果我们按那个价格卖打印机，我们真的会亏钱。

944
00:45:52.300 --> 00:45:53.460
I have a question.
我有个问题。

945
00:45:53.720 --> 00:45:53.960
Okay.
好的。

946
00:45:53.960 --> 00:45:56.380
I probably should have brought it up earlier.
我可能应该早点提出来的。

947
00:45:56.700 --> 00:45:59.060
How many printers is Donna buying?
唐娜要买多少台打印机？

948
00:45:59.380 --> 00:46:00.580
For her bar.
为了她的酒吧。

949
00:46:00.760 --> 00:46:02.840
That makes this whole day worth it.
这让这一整天都变得值得了。

950
00:46:03.100 --> 00:46:06.140
She manages one Sid and Dexter's.
她经营着一家叫“希德与德克斯特”的酒吧。

951
00:46:06.220 --> 00:46:08.220
I mean, how much printing are they doing?
我是说，他们到底要印多少东西？

952
00:46:08.520 --> 00:46:14.260
And then this made me think, like, in general, how does Saber stay in business?
然后这让我想到，总的来说，Saber 公司是怎么维持经营的？

953
00:46:14.520 --> 00:46:15.640
Like, paper.
比如纸张。

954
00:46:15.780 --> 00:46:18.360
You need paper on an ongoing basis.
你需要持续不断地购买纸张。

955
00:46:18.880 --> 00:46:19.760
But printers?
但打印机呢？

956
00:46:20.140 --> 00:46:23.900
I mean, how often are you reselling to the same clients?
我是说，你多久才能把东西再卖给同一批客户？

957
00:46:23.900 --> 00:46:27.040
It seems, like, very difficult.
这看起来非常困难。

958
00:46:27.560 --> 00:46:28.500
I don't know.
我不知道。

959
00:46:28.600 --> 00:46:33.600
The whole arc of Saber and their printers is just, like, literally falling apart for me all of a sudden.
Saber 公司和他们打印机的整个商业逻辑，对我来说突然间完全崩塌了。

960
00:46:33.860 --> 00:46:37.560
Well, you know, Pam is going to bring that up in some Pam sass.
嗯，你知道的，帕姆会用她那种刻薄劲儿把这事儿提出来。

961
00:46:37.660 --> 00:46:40.020
She's like, you can buy a printer over the phone.
她会说，你打个电话就能买台打印机。

962
00:46:40.560 --> 00:46:42.720
You can buy a printer at Best Buy.
你在百思买也能买到打印机。

963
00:46:43.080 --> 00:46:43.880
I know.
我知道。

964
00:46:44.160 --> 00:46:44.800
I mean.
我是说。

965
00:46:44.800 --> 00:46:45.680
I know.
我知道。

966
00:46:45.820 --> 00:46:49.120
You don't have to come in and make such a big show and presentation about it.
你没必要非得亲自跑过来，搞得这么大张旗鼓地做演示。

967
00:46:49.320 --> 00:46:54.800
I could see if we are supplying printers to all of AT&T.
如果我们要给整个美国电话电报公司供货，我还能理解。

968
00:46:54.940 --> 00:46:56.460
Or all of Sid and Dexter's.
或者给所有的 Sid and Dexter 连锁店。

969
00:46:56.520 --> 00:46:57.260
Maybe it's a chain.
也许那是个连锁店。

970
00:46:57.400 --> 00:46:59.000
Maybe there's going to be 300 printers.
也许会有三百台打印机。

971
00:46:59.180 --> 00:47:00.740
But I don't think Donna's in charge of that.
但我觉得唐娜不负责那个。

972
00:47:00.880 --> 00:47:02.160
No, she manages one.
不，她只管一家店。

973
00:47:02.740 --> 00:47:04.400
It's very odd to me.
这让我觉得非常奇怪。

974
00:47:04.860 --> 00:47:07.500
Let's go over and see what Kelly and Ryan are doing.
我们过去看看凯莉和瑞安在干什么。

975
00:47:08.100 --> 00:47:09.300
They're up to no good.
他们肯定没干好事。

976
00:47:09.680 --> 00:47:11.580
They're bullying someone online.
他们在网上欺负人呢。

977
00:47:11.580 --> 00:47:15.660
At 10 minutes and 32 seconds, you can see her typing on her computer.
在十分三十二秒的时候，你可以看到她在电脑上打字。

978
00:47:15.860 --> 00:47:21.880
That is a fake instant message account created by Henry Sane.
那是一个由亨利·塞恩创建的虚假即时通讯账号。

979
00:47:22.440 --> 00:47:23.460
I think that's number five.
我想那是第五个了。

980
00:47:24.600 --> 00:47:30.660
Well, Dwight is going to learn pretty quickly that having Kelly take that position might be worse than Daryl.
嗯，德怀特很快就会发现，让凯莉担任那个职位可能比达里尔还要糟糕。

981
00:47:30.660 --> 00:47:36.040
Because she says she's going to promote Ryan to manager, and then they're going to clean house.
因为她说她要提拔瑞安当经理，然后他们要进行大清洗。

982
00:47:36.700 --> 00:47:36.860
Yeah.
是啊。

983
00:47:37.460 --> 00:47:41.860
Well, Michael has so many people in the bullpen weighing in on this Donna thing.
迈克尔办公室里有太多人对唐娜这件事指手画脚了。

984
00:47:42.060 --> 00:47:42.380
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

985
00:47:42.820 --> 00:47:45.100
This starts the whole mint debate.
这就引发了关于薄荷糖的争论。

986
00:47:45.580 --> 00:47:48.580
Like, if you offer someone a mint and they say yes.
比如，如果你给某人一颗薄荷糖，他们答应了。

987
00:47:48.940 --> 00:47:49.260
Right.
没错。

988
00:47:49.380 --> 00:47:50.240
They might want to make out.
他们可能就是想跟你亲热。

989
00:47:50.360 --> 00:47:51.580
If they say no, they don't want to.
如果他们拒绝了，那就是不想。

990
00:47:52.100 --> 00:47:55.240
He's going to offer Donna a mint, then eat it off her hand.
他打算给唐娜一颗薄荷糖，然后直接从她手上吃掉。

991
00:47:55.240 --> 00:47:57.440
We had a fan question from Stacey C.
我们收到了来自北卡罗来纳州夏洛特市的粉丝斯泰西·C的提问。

992
00:47:57.540 --> 00:47:58.840
in Charlotte, North Carolina.
在北卡罗来纳州夏洛特市。

993
00:47:59.240 --> 00:48:03.960
Was Michael eating the mint from the palm of Donna's hand improvised?
迈克尔从唐娜手心里吃薄荷糖是即兴发挥的吗？

994
00:48:03.960 --> 00:48:06.460
Because her reaction looks truly surprised.
因为她的反应看起来真的很惊讶。

995
00:48:07.500 --> 00:48:13.520
I'll tell you, it was not improvised, but it was also not the original idea in the script.
我告诉你，那不是即兴发挥，但也不是剧本里最初的想法。

996
00:48:14.820 --> 00:48:16.260
Originally, it's worse.
最初的想法更糟糕。

997
00:48:16.540 --> 00:48:21.620
He was going to put the mint into her mouth very sensually.
他本来是要非常性感地把薄荷糖放进她嘴里。

998
00:48:21.860 --> 00:48:22.560
Oh, gosh.
天哪。

999
00:48:23.140 --> 00:48:31.360
On the day, they liked the idea that she would reciprocate the mint, you know, where she eats the mint, and then she's like,
拍摄当天，他们更喜欢她回请薄荷糖的想法，你知道的，就是她吃了一颗薄荷糖，然后她就像是，

1000
00:48:31.480 --> 00:48:34.360
do you want a mint that's going to make Michael think?
你要来一颗吗，这会让迈克尔怎么想？

1001
00:48:34.760 --> 00:48:35.080
Uh-huh.
嗯哼。

1002
00:48:35.280 --> 00:48:38.980
Like, oh, it's on, and then he would eat the mint off her hand.
就像，哦，开始了，然后他会从她手上吃掉薄荷糖。

1003
00:48:39.560 --> 00:48:42.640
This is going to bring a meeting in the kitchen.
这会引发一场厨房会议。

1004
00:48:43.220 --> 00:48:45.880
It also brings one of my favorite lines.
这也引出了我最喜欢的台词之一。

1005
00:48:46.500 --> 00:48:47.640
Which one is it?
是哪一句？

1006
00:48:47.960 --> 00:48:49.740
Why don't you just shut up?
你为什么不闭嘴呢？

1007
00:48:49.940 --> 00:48:50.460
Yes.
是的。

1008
00:48:50.460 --> 00:48:52.700
Well, why don't you shut up?
那么，你为什么不闭嘴呢？

1009
00:48:53.140 --> 00:48:55.500
Kevin yells that at 12 minutes, 3 seconds.
凯文在12分03秒时喊出了那句话。

1010
00:48:55.740 --> 00:48:56.840
It's also mine.
那也是我最喜欢的。

1011
00:48:56.840 --> 00:49:01.880
And I want to point out, it sounded exactly like Brian and not like Kevin.
而且我想指出，听起来完全像布莱恩，而不像凯文。

1012
00:49:02.060 --> 00:49:02.700
You think?
你觉得吗？

1013
00:49:02.920 --> 00:49:03.260
Yes.
是的。

1014
00:49:03.520 --> 00:49:04.760
Oh, can we hear it?
哦，我们能听听吗？

1015
00:49:05.320 --> 00:49:07.220
Well, why don't you just move the M&M's?
好吧，你为什么不把M&M豆移开呢？

1016
00:49:07.220 --> 00:49:08.560
Well, why don't you shut up?
好吧，你为什么不闭嘴呢？

1017
00:49:09.040 --> 00:49:10.980
Come on, that sounded just like Brian.
得了吧，那听起来简直就是布莱恩。

1018
00:49:11.120 --> 00:49:11.720
I guess.
我猜吧。

1019
00:49:12.320 --> 00:49:13.460
That is Brian.
那就是布莱恩。

1020
00:49:13.660 --> 00:49:15.540
That is, I don't think that's Kevin's voice.
那是，我不觉得那是凯文的声音。

1021
00:49:16.380 --> 00:49:23.720
Well, during this whole scene, everybody is trying to tell Michael to stop, that Donna does not like him back.
嗯，在整个场景中，每个人都在试图告诉迈克尔停下来，说唐娜并不喜欢他。

1022
00:49:24.000 --> 00:49:28.480
And then Pam is like, no.
然后帕姆说，不。

1023
00:49:29.160 --> 00:49:34.780
Lady, I went to the message boards to see what fans thought of this episode at the time that it aired.
女士，我去了留言板，看看粉丝们在这一集播出时是怎么想的。

1024
00:49:34.780 --> 00:49:37.900
And there were three things that got the most mentions.
有三件事被提及得最多。

1025
00:49:38.300 --> 00:49:38.440
What?
什么？

1026
00:49:39.020 --> 00:49:42.960
One, people loved when Kevin yells at Andy about his M&Ms.
第一，人们喜欢凯文对安迪大喊关于他M&M豆的事。

1027
00:49:44.340 --> 00:49:49.600
Second, people did not think that Pam was acting the same in this episode.
第二，人们认为帕姆在这一集里的表现不太一样。

1028
00:49:50.140 --> 00:49:50.500
Oh.
哦。

1029
00:49:51.700 --> 00:49:56.580
Nick said, am I the only one that thinks Pam was really weird in tonight's episode?
尼克说，难道只有我觉得帕姆在今晚这一集里真的很奇怪吗？

1030
00:49:56.760 --> 00:49:59.860
Not only the way that she was acting, but how she looked, too.
不仅是她的行为举止，还有她的样子也是。

1031
00:50:00.660 --> 00:50:05.260
Sombreros Are Love said, I completely agree with whoever said Pam was weird.
“草帽即是爱”说，我完全同意那些说帕姆很奇怪的人。

1032
00:50:05.880 --> 00:50:10.500
Megan said, I'm worried they're taking Jim and Pam in a weird direction, mainly Pam.
梅根说，我很担心他们把吉姆和帕姆带向一个奇怪的方向，主要是帕姆。

1033
00:50:11.200 --> 00:50:11.680
Wow.
哇。

1034
00:50:12.060 --> 00:50:16.360
But then Sarah defended Pam by saying, how is she acting weird?
但后来莎拉为帕姆辩护说，她哪里表现得奇怪了？

1035
00:50:16.560 --> 00:50:18.520
She was trying to help Michael with his love life.
她是在试图帮助迈克尔处理他的感情生活。

1036
00:50:18.520 --> 00:50:24.760
And Megan agreed, saying Pam always has a soft spot for Michael's love life and is advising him on what to do.
梅根表示同意，说帕姆对迈克尔的感情生活总是心软，并且在给他出谋划策。

1037
00:50:25.100 --> 00:50:25.960
What do you think?
你怎么看？

1038
00:50:26.060 --> 00:50:26.940
Did you think it was weird?
你觉得这很奇怪吗？

1039
00:50:29.330 --> 00:50:35.290
I guess the only part that was weird for me is how long she stuck in there with him.
我想对我来说唯一奇怪的部分是她坚持陪他待了那么久。

1040
00:50:36.170 --> 00:50:36.610
Pam?
帕姆吗？

1041
00:50:36.770 --> 00:50:36.990
Yeah.
是的。

1042
00:50:37.470 --> 00:50:41.690
Like, in the beginning of the episode, all the information is new.
就像，在这一集的开头，所有的信息都是新的。

1043
00:50:41.790 --> 00:50:44.930
So I could see her being like, well, you know, guys, we don't know.
所以我能理解她会说，嗯，你知道，伙计们，我们不知道。

1044
00:50:45.170 --> 00:50:46.130
Maybe she likes him.
也许她喜欢他。

1045
00:50:46.190 --> 00:50:48.110
I mean, she's here, right?
我是说，她人在这儿，对吧？

1046
00:50:48.530 --> 00:50:48.910
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1047
00:50:48.910 --> 00:51:00.110
But I felt like, as the day went, how I normally associate Pam as, like, the voice of reason would have been like, Michael, I take it all back.
但我感觉，随着时间推移，按照我通常对帕姆作为“理性之声”的印象，她本应该说，迈克尔，我收回刚才的话。

1048
00:51:00.270 --> 00:51:01.830
She's just pumped the brakes.
她只是踩了刹车。

1049
00:51:03.070 --> 00:51:15.670
As Jenna, when I was watching this episode, as soon as I kind of saw her, like, manipulating him, like, taking off her extra jacket, I started to think, oh,
作为珍娜，当我在看这一集时，当我看到她像是在操纵他，比如脱掉她多余的外套时，我就开始想，哦，

1050
00:51:15.810 --> 00:51:16.730
that's what's happening.
原来是这么回事。

1051
00:51:16.990 --> 00:51:18.850
She wants a discount on her printer.
她想给她的打印机打个折。

1052
00:51:19.030 --> 00:51:19.350
Right.
没错。

1053
00:51:19.510 --> 00:51:19.690
Yeah.
是啊。

1054
00:51:19.750 --> 00:51:21.830
And she's just flirting for that reason.
而且她就是为了这个才在那儿献殷勤。

1055
00:51:22.090 --> 00:51:25.110
But I would like to say, Pam didn't see that.
但我得说，帕姆没看出来。

1056
00:51:25.110 --> 00:51:28.050
I, as a viewer, saw that, but Pam doesn't know that, right?
作为观众的我看到了，但帕姆不知道，对吧？

1057
00:51:28.510 --> 00:51:34.230
So she's still thinking, maybe she's there for Michael, not for a printer.
所以她还在想，也许她是冲着迈克尔来的，而不是为了打印机。

1058
00:51:34.930 --> 00:51:43.830
Anyway, finally, a lot of people on the message boards mentioned that they didn't get any new information on the Andy Aaron storyline.
总之，最后，很多留言板上的网友提到，他们没能从安迪和亚伦的故事线里得到任何新消息。

1059
00:51:43.830 --> 00:51:49.690
And they were very disappointed, you know, because they had a very big breakup last week.
他们非常失望，你知道的，因为上周他们刚经历了一场大分手。

1060
00:51:49.690 --> 00:51:53.330
And they would have liked to have seen some mention of it.
他们本来希望能看到一些相关的交代。

1061
00:51:53.590 --> 00:51:56.790
You know, I think they're not going to get much next week either.
你知道，我觉得下周他们也不会有什么进展。

1062
00:51:57.090 --> 00:52:01.810
Well, you know, there actually is a scene between Andy and Aaron that would have been in next week's episode.
嗯，其实安迪和亚伦之间确实有一场戏，本来是会出现在下周剧集里的。

1063
00:52:01.810 --> 00:52:03.170
It's in the deleted scenes.
那是在删减片段里。

1064
00:52:03.330 --> 00:52:04.350
I'll share it next week.
我下周会分享出来。

1065
00:52:04.490 --> 00:52:05.490
Oh, all right.
哦，好吧。

1066
00:52:05.750 --> 00:52:10.370
Well, Dwight is still freaking out about the idea of Kelly and Ryan running things.
德怀特还在为凯莉和瑞安要掌权的事抓狂。

1067
00:52:10.370 --> 00:52:12.090
He bursts into Gabe's office.
他冲进了盖博的办公室。

1068
00:52:12.630 --> 00:52:16.850
And this is when he finds out that Daryl has withdrawn his application.
就在这时，他发现达里尔撤回了申请。

1069
00:52:16.850 --> 00:52:19.890
He says he has a scheduling conflict with softball.
他说他因为垒球比赛的时间冲突。

1070
00:52:20.530 --> 00:52:26.510
Yeah, Daryl says he has his whole life to be a minority executive, but he only has about one year left in his knees.
是啊，达里尔说他这辈子有的是时间当少数族裔高管，但他的膝盖只剩一年左右的运动寿命了。

1071
00:52:26.810 --> 00:52:29.330
Kelly is now the only applicant.
凯莉现在是唯一的申请人了。

1072
00:52:30.130 --> 00:52:30.650
Yeah.
没错。

1073
00:52:31.150 --> 00:52:34.110
And she is going to walk into her interview with Gabe.
她准备去参加盖博的面试了。

1074
00:52:34.310 --> 00:52:36.270
She's wearing a beautiful sari.
她穿了一件漂亮的纱丽。

1075
00:52:36.650 --> 00:52:37.010
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1076
00:52:37.450 --> 00:52:40.850
Gabe asks her about the bindi that is on her forehead.
盖博问起她额头上的吉祥痣。

1077
00:52:41.250 --> 00:52:43.430
She says she's offended by the question.
她说她被这个问题冒犯了。

1078
00:52:44.010 --> 00:52:44.990
She won't answer.
她拒绝回答。

1079
00:52:44.990 --> 00:52:48.190
But Kelly will tell Gabe about all of her hobbies.
但凯莉会跟盖博大谈特谈她的各种爱好。

1080
00:52:48.670 --> 00:52:53.730
And in the middle of this, Dwight is going to return with a new applicant, and it is Hide.
就在这期间，德怀特带了一位新申请人回来，是海德。

1081
00:52:54.170 --> 00:53:01.290
He tells Hide to share his life story, and Hide begins his same monologue that he gave in Happy Hour.
他让海德分享他的人生故事，于是海德开始背诵他在《欢乐时光》那一集里的独白。

1082
00:53:01.430 --> 00:53:02.310
It delighted me.
这让我很开心。

1083
00:53:02.310 --> 00:53:08.430
I asked Hide what it was like doing that amazing talking head in Happy Hour, and here's what he said.
我问海德在《欢乐时光》里做那个精彩的访谈镜头是什么感觉，他是这么说的。

1084
00:53:08.850 --> 00:53:18.210
I actually did not get a lot of time to think about the big speech for the episode since I got five different variations of my speech at around 10 p.m.
其实我没多少时间去构思那集的大段台词，因为我在前一天晚上10点左右才拿到五个不同版本的演讲稿。

1085
00:53:18.670 --> 00:53:19.410
the day before.
也就是拍摄前一天。

1086
00:53:19.410 --> 00:53:20.630
Oh, my gosh.
天哪。

1087
00:53:20.870 --> 00:53:21.270
Yeah.
是啊。

1088
00:53:21.990 --> 00:53:25.350
I desperately tried to memorize all five variations.
我拼命想把这五个版本全背下来。

1089
00:53:26.170 --> 00:53:29.130
When I went to the rehearsal, I completely forgot everything.
结果去排练的时候，我全忘了。

1090
00:53:29.390 --> 00:53:37.030
He went on to say that he decided he was going to work hard to memorize all the different variations so that he'd be ready to go on the shoot day.
他接着说，他决定努力把所有不同版本都背下来，这样拍摄当天就能准备就绪。

1091
00:53:37.330 --> 00:53:42.570
When the day came to actually film the scene, he said he was able to say his lines perfectly, and he said,
当真正拍摄那场戏的那天到来时，他说他能完美地说出台词，他说，

1092
00:53:42.570 --> 00:53:46.430
I remember I was so happy I was able to do it on the first take or two.
我记得当时特别高兴，因为我一两次就拍过了。

1093
00:53:46.650 --> 00:53:47.670
I love it.
我太喜欢了。

1094
00:53:47.770 --> 00:53:48.730
He nailed it.
他演得太棒了。

1095
00:53:48.930 --> 00:53:49.710
Totally nailed it.
简直绝了。

1096
00:53:49.710 --> 00:53:50.710
I mean, it's so good.
我是说，真的太精彩了。

1097
00:53:51.030 --> 00:53:55.170
I also asked Hide if he still gets recognized for his role in the office.
我还问了海德，他现在还会因为在《办公室》里的角色被认出来吗？

1098
00:53:55.510 --> 00:53:58.490
He said yes, and he has a very sweet story to share.
他说会，而且他有一个很暖心的故事要分享。

1099
00:53:58.890 --> 00:54:06.630
He said, after doing the big heart surgeon speech, I started to get some people in the street randomly asking me if I was the guy from the office.
他说，在做了那个关于心脏外科医生的长篇演讲后，开始有路人随机问我是不是《办公室》里的那个人。

1100
00:54:07.150 --> 00:54:11.410
I was very surprised because I had no idea the show was so popular at the time.
我非常惊讶，因为我当时根本不知道这部剧这么火。

1101
00:54:11.410 --> 00:54:18.130
I remember I had to quickly come up with a fancy autograph because I never thought I would have people asking me for autographs.
我记得我当时得赶紧想出一个花哨的签名，因为我从没想过会有人找我要签名。

1102
00:54:18.450 --> 00:54:22.130
But his favorite time getting recognized, he said, was by a fan.
但他提到，他最喜欢的一次被认出来的经历，是一位粉丝给他的。

1103
00:54:22.270 --> 00:54:30.090
It was a little kid who did the signature, the best, double thumbs up to him without saying a word while I was in the supermarket.
当时我在超市，有个小孩子认出了我，他什么话也没说，直接对我竖起了两个大拇指。

1104
00:54:30.330 --> 00:54:31.990
Oh, I love that.
噢，我太喜欢这个了。

1105
00:54:32.830 --> 00:54:37.910
The last question I asked Hide was if he took anything from set when the show was over.
我问Hide的最后一个问题是，剧集结束后他有没有从片场拿走什么东西。

1106
00:54:37.910 --> 00:54:44.070
He said he wasn't there on the last episode, but he did receive an official jacket after the show wrapped.
他说最后一集他不在场，但剧集杀青后他确实收到了一件官方夹克。

1107
00:54:44.310 --> 00:54:51.230
He said it was a really nice jacket, and one day a fan wanted it so badly that I autographed it and I gave it away.
他说那件夹克真的很棒，有一天一位粉丝非常想要，我就给它签了名并送给了他。

1108
00:54:51.650 --> 00:54:53.110
He's the sweetest person.
他真是个最贴心的人。

1109
00:54:53.790 --> 00:54:54.670
So lovely.
太可爱了。

1110
00:54:55.110 --> 00:55:00.210
He said that he was hoping to get the warehouse worker uniform that he wore during the show,
他说他本来希望能拿到他在剧中穿的那套仓库员工制服，

1111
00:55:00.730 --> 00:55:06.150
but he was informed by a fan that his uniform was sold at the NBC auction.
但有粉丝告诉他，他的制服在NBC的拍卖会上被卖掉了。

1112
00:55:06.750 --> 00:55:13.010
So he tried his best to bid on it so he could get it, but unfortunately he was outbid in the end.
于是他尽力去竞拍，想把它买回来，但遗憾的是最后还是被别人拍走了。

1113
00:55:13.570 --> 00:55:15.070
But he goes on to say,
但他接着说，

1114
00:55:15.350 --> 00:55:20.430
I'm happy someone liked my role so much that they fought really hard for the uniform,
我很高兴有人那么喜欢我的角色，以至于他们为了这套制服如此努力地竞拍，

1115
00:55:20.430 --> 00:55:22.710
and it's in the hands of a happy fan.
而且它现在落到了一位开心的粉丝手中。

1116
00:55:23.250 --> 00:55:29.350
Well, Hide, I think that is such a sweet point of view on a story that just kind of made me mad.
好吧，Hide，我觉得你对这件事的看法真是太暖心了，虽然这事儿刚开始让我挺生气的。

1117
00:55:29.350 --> 00:55:30.170
I know.
我懂。

1118
00:55:30.310 --> 00:55:31.690
I want Hide to have his uniform.
我真希望Hide能拥有他的制服。

1119
00:55:32.170 --> 00:55:33.990
Isn't he on Cameo, Ange?
他在Cameo上有账号吗，Ange？

1120
00:55:34.090 --> 00:55:35.110
Yes, he is.
是的，他有。

1121
00:55:35.610 --> 00:55:40.290
Yeah, Cameo is the place where you can find different celebrities and public figures,
没错，Cameo是一个你可以找到各种名人和公众人物的平台，

1122
00:55:40.310 --> 00:55:43.390
and you pay a small fee, and they'll make a personal video for you.
你支付一小笔费用，他们就会为你录制一段个人视频。

1123
00:55:43.590 --> 00:55:46.730
Yes, Hide shared with us that he just started doing Cameo for fun,
是的，Hide跟我们分享说他刚开始玩Cameo纯粹是为了好玩，

1124
00:55:46.830 --> 00:55:50.570
but if anyone wants a personal video message of him as his character,
但如果有人想要他以剧中角色的身份录制个人视频留言，

1125
00:55:50.850 --> 00:55:52.710
you can go to Cameo and find him.
你可以去Cameo上找他。

1126
00:55:53.330 --> 00:56:01.470
He is also on Instagram at Hidetoshimura, H-I-D-E-T-O-S-H-I-I-M-U-R-A,
他也在Instagram上，账号是Hidetoshimura，拼写是H-I-D-E-T-O-S-H-I-I-M-U-R-A，

1127
00:56:01.670 --> 00:56:02.950
and you can follow him there.
你可以在那里关注他。

1128
00:56:03.110 --> 00:56:04.530
He says he posts pretty often.
他说他更新得挺频繁的。

1129
00:56:05.570 --> 00:56:06.910
Thank you so much, Hide.
非常感谢你，Hide。

1130
00:56:07.150 --> 00:56:07.790
Thank you.
谢谢。

1131
00:56:08.030 --> 00:56:09.830
I'm so glad we got in touch with him.
我很高兴我们联系上了他。

1132
00:56:10.250 --> 00:56:11.710
Good job, Ange.
干得好，Ange。

1133
00:56:11.890 --> 00:56:12.150
Aw.
噢。

1134
00:56:12.150 --> 00:56:17.650
Well, I guess Donna has finally purchased her printer, printers.
好吧，我想Donna终于买下她的打印机了，是打印机们。

1135
00:56:18.090 --> 00:56:19.170
How many did she need?
她到底需要多少台？

1136
00:56:19.170 --> 00:56:21.210
We don't know, but the deal is done.
我们不知道，但交易完成了。

1137
00:56:21.490 --> 00:56:25.310
Michael is going to walk her out very awkwardly.
Michael正以一种非常尴尬的方式送她出去。

1138
00:56:25.510 --> 00:56:26.950
There's an awkward hug.
有一个尴尬的拥抱。

1139
00:56:27.170 --> 00:56:31.730
He follows her all the way to nearly the elevators.
他一直跟着她，几乎送到了电梯口。

1140
00:56:32.070 --> 00:56:32.330
Yes.
是的。

1141
00:56:32.770 --> 00:56:35.050
By the way, at 15 minutes and 11 seconds,
顺便说一下，在15分11秒的时候，

1142
00:56:35.490 --> 00:56:38.350
remember last time I was talking about the picture?
还记得上次我提到的那张画吗？

1143
00:56:38.530 --> 00:56:39.290
That big print?
就是那幅大画？

1144
00:56:39.570 --> 00:56:39.790
Yes.
对。

1145
00:56:39.790 --> 00:56:41.950
I got a closer look at it.
我仔细看了一下。

1146
00:56:42.150 --> 00:56:44.510
It's a valley of trees with a waterfall.
那是一片有瀑布的树林山谷。

1147
00:56:44.970 --> 00:56:46.710
So I got closure on that.
所以我终于解开了这个心结。

1148
00:56:46.870 --> 00:56:47.830
Okay, I'm really glad.
好的，我真为你感到高兴。

1149
00:56:47.830 --> 00:56:49.070
I appreciated it.
我很感激你告诉我。

1150
00:56:49.410 --> 00:56:50.690
Michael's pretty glum now.
Michael现在看起来挺沮丧的。

1151
00:56:50.870 --> 00:56:51.030
Yeah.
是啊。

1152
00:56:51.290 --> 00:56:52.090
Donna's gone.
唐娜走了。

1153
00:56:52.490 --> 00:56:54.830
He says he can't trust his own feelings anymore.
他说他再也无法相信自己的感觉了。

1154
00:56:55.610 --> 00:56:57.570
And everyone's weighing in on it.
每个人都在对此发表意见。

1155
00:56:57.710 --> 00:57:00.730
And he comes in with, you know, when I tore my scrote.
然后他进来的时候，你知道的，当时我撕裂了阴囊。

1156
00:57:01.010 --> 00:57:01.450
Yeah.
是啊。

1157
00:57:01.570 --> 00:57:05.810
I was seeing a hot urologist, and I thought she was into me.
我当时在看一位性感的泌尿科医生，我以为她对我有意思。

1158
00:57:05.890 --> 00:57:07.050
It gets confusing down there.
那下面确实容易让人困惑。

1159
00:57:07.230 --> 00:57:09.370
I have a fan catch from Sergio P.
我收到一条来自墨西哥塞尔吉奥·P的粉丝发现。

1160
00:57:09.690 --> 00:57:10.510
in Mexico.
在墨西哥。

1161
00:57:10.510 --> 00:57:13.370
I wonder if Sergio and I have the same catch.
我不知道我和塞尔吉奥发现的是不是同一个。

1162
00:57:13.930 --> 00:57:18.970
Does it happen at 17 minutes and 18 seconds, and does it involve Pam's desk?
是不是发生在17分18秒，而且和帕姆的桌子有关？

1163
00:57:19.450 --> 00:57:20.010
No.
不是。

1164
00:57:20.310 --> 00:57:21.010
What is it?
那是什么？

1165
00:57:21.290 --> 00:57:21.750
All right.
好吧。

1166
00:57:22.090 --> 00:57:28.330
Sergio said, if you look under Pam's desk, there's a piece of masking tape on it that says Pam.
塞尔吉奥说，如果你看帕姆的桌子下面，上面有一块写着“帕姆”的遮蔽胶带。

1167
00:57:28.330 --> 00:57:33.490
He said, is that because you would move the set around and take out the desks?
他说，那是因为你们会移动布景并把桌子搬走吗？

1168
00:57:33.610 --> 00:57:34.970
What a great catch!
真是个伟大的发现！

1169
00:57:36.470 --> 00:57:37.030
Yes!
没错！

1170
00:57:37.410 --> 00:57:38.890
That's exactly why.
正是因为这个。

1171
00:57:39.090 --> 00:57:41.270
Sergio, I live for that catch.
塞尔吉奥，我就是为了这种发现而活的。

1172
00:57:41.390 --> 00:57:42.070
What's yours?
你发现的是什么？

1173
00:57:42.510 --> 00:57:45.210
Mine is at 18 minutes, 7 seconds.
我的是在18分7秒。

1174
00:57:45.430 --> 00:57:47.250
What's up with the stains on the wall?
墙上的污渍是怎么回事？

1175
00:57:48.110 --> 00:57:49.190
Stains on the wall?
墙上的污渍？

1176
00:57:49.190 --> 00:57:55.650
Oh, there are two stains on the wall by Michael's left shoulder as he is sitting in the chair.
哦，迈克尔坐在椅子上时，他左肩旁边的墙上有两块污渍。

1177
00:57:56.030 --> 00:57:56.830
Two stains.
两块污渍。

1178
00:57:57.030 --> 00:57:57.150
Yeah.
是啊。

1179
00:57:57.270 --> 00:57:57.870
No, it's gross.
不，太恶心了。

1180
00:57:58.010 --> 00:57:59.070
What do they look like?
它们看起来像什么？

1181
00:57:59.250 --> 00:58:00.370
Do they look like hands?
看起来像手印吗？

1182
00:58:00.610 --> 00:58:01.590
Do they look like what?
看起来像什么？

1183
00:58:01.990 --> 00:58:05.610
I don't know if this is because I was eating barbecue chips at the time.
我不知道是不是因为我当时在吃烧烤味薯片。

1184
00:58:05.610 --> 00:58:09.790
They look like when my kids wipe barbecue chip hands on things.
它们看起来就像我孩子吃完烧烤味薯片后在东西上擦手留下的痕迹。

1185
00:58:10.090 --> 00:58:10.610
Oh, gosh.
天哪。

1186
00:58:10.730 --> 00:58:10.930
Yeah.
是啊。

1187
00:58:11.550 --> 00:58:12.010
Gross.
恶心。

1188
00:58:12.010 --> 00:58:12.710
I know.
我知道。

1189
00:58:13.010 --> 00:58:13.650
I know.
我知道。

1190
00:58:13.710 --> 00:58:15.070
It's all I could look at.
我当时只能盯着那个看。

1191
00:58:15.390 --> 00:58:18.130
Well, two more things are going to happen in this scene.
好吧，这一幕里还会发生两件事。

1192
00:58:18.670 --> 00:58:23.110
Gabe announces that Kelly is the newest member of the minority executive program,
盖博宣布凯莉是少数族裔高管培训项目的最新成员，

1193
00:58:23.630 --> 00:58:27.690
and Erin finds Donna's hair clip that she left behind.
然后艾琳发现了唐娜落下的发夹。

1194
00:58:28.490 --> 00:58:28.810
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1195
00:58:28.990 --> 00:58:30.310
Michael thinks it's a sign.
迈克尔觉得这是一个信号。

1196
00:58:30.510 --> 00:58:32.010
She left it on purpose.
她是故意留下的。

1197
00:58:32.350 --> 00:58:32.690
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1198
00:58:32.690 --> 00:58:35.190
Everyone is like, no, no, no, Michael, no.
大家都说，不，不，不，迈克尔，别这样。

1199
00:58:35.770 --> 00:58:37.710
But he's going to run out to give it to her.
但他还是会跑出去把它还给她。

1200
00:58:37.850 --> 00:58:38.570
He is.
他会的。

1201
00:58:38.730 --> 00:58:39.550
And guess what?
你猜怎么着？

1202
00:58:39.790 --> 00:58:41.390
She says, Michael, you were right.
她说，迈克尔，你是对的。

1203
00:58:41.390 --> 00:58:43.510
And she pulls him in for a big kiss.
然后她把他拉过去深情一吻。

1204
00:58:43.750 --> 00:58:48.050
And all I could think of was, Donna, this is a documentary.
我当时满脑子想的都是，唐娜，这可是纪录片啊。

1205
00:58:48.710 --> 00:58:50.570
It's going to air at some point.
迟早是要播出的。

1206
00:58:51.230 --> 00:58:53.010
We'll get to that next week.
我们下周会聊到这个。

1207
00:58:53.130 --> 00:58:54.230
We sure will.
肯定会聊的。

1208
00:58:54.370 --> 00:58:56.410
But this was a bit of a spy shot.
但这算是个偷拍镜头。

1209
00:58:56.550 --> 00:58:59.190
So I believe it that she didn't see the camera.
所以我相信她确实没看到摄像机。

1210
00:58:59.330 --> 00:58:59.950
I believe it.
我相信。

1211
00:58:59.990 --> 00:59:03.410
It was from the office window pointing down into the parking lot.
那是从办公室窗户往下拍到停车场的。

1212
00:59:03.570 --> 00:59:06.670
Well, next week, we're going to find out why she had to be so coy.
嗯，下周我们会找出她为什么表现得那么矜持。

1213
00:59:06.970 --> 00:59:07.590
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1214
00:59:07.590 --> 00:59:15.890
Like, around others, around the cameras, how she could only admit her true feelings for Michael when she thought they were alone.
比如在别人面前，在镜头前，她只有在以为两人独处时才敢承认对迈克尔的真实感情。

1215
00:59:16.090 --> 00:59:16.510
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1216
00:59:16.610 --> 00:59:18.950
I mean, it's literally the plot of next week's episode.
我是说，这简直就是下集剧情的梗概。

1217
00:59:19.670 --> 00:59:23.190
Michael's going to come back to the office where Kelly is gloating.
迈克尔回到办公室，凯莉正在那儿幸灾乐祸。

1218
00:59:23.770 --> 00:59:25.390
She tells Aaron, you know what?
她告诉亚伦，你知道吗？

1219
00:59:25.390 --> 00:59:29.370
She gets a stipend to buy all new clothes and Aaron can have, like, any of her old stuff.
她有一笔津贴可以买全新的衣服，而亚伦可以买她任何旧衣服。

1220
00:59:29.370 --> 00:59:30.730
That she can buy them.
她是说亚伦可以买。

1221
00:59:31.110 --> 00:59:31.550
Yeah.
是啊。

1222
00:59:31.690 --> 00:59:32.950
She's not giving them to Aaron.
她不是要送给亚伦。

1223
00:59:33.230 --> 00:59:34.330
Aaron can buy them.
亚伦可以买。

1224
00:59:34.470 --> 00:59:37.610
And she means any of the clothes she was going to give to Goodwill anyway.
而且她指的是那些她本来就要捐给慈善机构的衣服。

1225
00:59:37.850 --> 00:59:37.990
Right.
没错。

1226
00:59:38.070 --> 00:59:39.150
But Aaron can pay her for him.
但亚伦得付钱买。

1227
00:59:39.310 --> 00:59:39.590
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1228
00:59:40.090 --> 00:59:41.370
Michael can't help himself.
迈克尔忍不住了。

1229
00:59:41.810 --> 00:59:45.430
He's going to tell everyone what just happened, but no one believes him.
他要把刚才发生的事告诉所有人，但没人相信他。

1230
00:59:45.550 --> 00:59:45.810
Nope.
没错。

1231
00:59:46.130 --> 00:59:49.490
And he says it doesn't matter if they believe him or not because he knows it happened.
他说别人信不信都无所谓，因为他自己知道发生了什么。

1232
00:59:49.670 --> 00:59:50.750
Also, I did it!
而且，我做到了！

1233
00:59:52.290 --> 00:59:54.150
And that is the end of the episode.
这就是这一集的结尾。

1234
00:59:54.610 --> 00:59:57.350
Thank you guys so much for re-watching with us.
非常感谢大家和我们一起重温。

1235
00:59:57.350 --> 00:59:59.330
Thank you to Hede and to Randy.
感谢希德和兰迪。

1236
01:00:00.030 --> 01:00:03.450
And thanks to Audrey for some fun stings.
也感谢奥黛丽提供的有趣转场音效。

1237
01:00:03.770 --> 01:00:04.010
Yeah.
是啊。

1238
01:00:04.230 --> 01:00:07.290
We will be back next week with the cover-up.
下周我们将回来聊聊掩盖真相的事。

1239
01:00:07.470 --> 01:00:08.370
See you then.
到时候见。

1240
